<vertex eid="3"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered Yes" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">C01 [YES]
Selected contacts have verified endpoints?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">C01 | Selected contacts have verified endpoints?

Status: YES

Method: Structural dissection / anatomical identity

Scope / coordinates: The retained verified set only: annotations 124698307 (EE), 65017731 (EI), 8105899 (IE).

Remaining search space: Both endpoints have accepted identity/spatial support for each selected contact, or at least one lacks it.

Binary predicate: Each contact in the stated retained set passes the recorded endpoint identity and spatial checks.

Decision limit: Use saved exact identity and 5-voxel endpoint audit criteria; proximity alone is insufficient.

Recorded observation: The completed 3000-sample summary retains three verified anatomical contacts; new candidates did not enlarge the set.

YES: Check cable support per contact before simulation.

NO: Retain unsupported contact candidates outside the verified simulation graph.

Next check: Keep IDs, sending/receiving cell and component support; do not treat the partial map as complete connectivity.

Unresolved after either answer: The answer applies to this selected set, not every exported candidate or every biological connection.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/h01-network.md
docs/evidence/h01-endpoint-recheck-5voxel-3000.json

